Rule 1 (tensor shapes should be the same)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
>>
Rule 2 (v_2 should be a valid dimension of input tensor)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= -1 × ndim(v_1) ≤ v_2 ∧ v_2 ≤ ndim(v_1) - 1
>>
Rule 3 (input tensor is empty or only contains non-negative values)
{v_1 : tensor} |= (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = 0) ∨ min(v_1) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 4 (broadcasting compatibility for tensor shapes)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, if ndim(v_1) ≥ ndim(v_2) then ndim(v_1) - 1 else ndim(v_2) - 1] : ndim(v_1) - i - 1 < 0 ∨ ndim(v_2) - i - 1 < 0 ∨ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - i - 1) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - i - 1) = 1 ∨ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - i - 1) = shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - i - 1)
>>
Rule 5 (Integer indices only valid with int-compatible dtype)
{v_1 : tuple(int), v_2 : dtype} |= ∀i ∈ [0, v_1.len - 1] : v_1[i] ≥ 0 ∧ v_2 = 1 ∨ v_2 = 2 ∨ v_2 = 3 ∨ v_2 = 4 ∨ v_2 = 5
